---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import site from "../../site.config.mjs";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About Vectorpost and its relationship with OnlyOrders."
>
  <article>
    <h1>About Vectorpost</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Vectorpost is a blog about content operations, retrieval, and search for
      e-commerce teams.
    </p>

    <p>
      We write about publishing workflows, structuring product content for
      machines and people, and the retrieval systems that decide whether useful
      content ever gets found. Most of that work happens quietly — in CMS
      pipelines, metadata schemas, and search relevance tuning — which is exactly
      why it deserves a space where it can be discussed openly.
    </p>

    <div class="notice">
      <strong>Disclosure:</strong> Vectorpost is operated by{" "}
      <a href="https://onlyorders.tech" rel="nofollow">OnlyOrders</a>{" "}
      (onlyorders.tech), a company building AI auto-reply and chat-order tools
      for e-commerce across Messenger, WhatsApp, and Instagram. See our{" "}
      <a href="/onlyorders/">OnlyOrders hub</a> for an overview of the product.
      This blog is published for educational and SEO purposes. It is not an
      independent journalism outlet, and it does not present itself as one.
    </div>

    <h2>Why the name?</h2>
    <p>
      "Vectorpost" is a nod to retrieval and embeddings — the idea that content
      becomes more useful when it can be represented, matched, and routed to the
      right person at the right moment. We use that lens for everything we
      discuss here: text structures, metadata, publishing cadence, and the
      systems that sit between a post and a purchase.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
    <p>
      Articles are written by the {site.author}. We aim for sourced facts where
      possible and clearly mark analysis or opinion as such. We do not publish
      affiliate promo content, and we keep mentions of the parent company sparse
      and relevant.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For corrections or questions, reach out through the parent site,{" "}
      <a href="https://onlyorders.tech" rel="nofollow">onlyorders.tech</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
